### Creating and Using Landlock Scope Flags

Source: https://docs.rs/landlock/0.4.3/src/landlock/scope.rs.html

Demonstrates how to create a `BitFlags<Scope>` set for signals and abstract Unix sockets, and how to compare it with a set created using `Scope::from_all`.

```rust
use landlock::{ABI, Access, Scope, BitFlags, make_bitflags};

let signal = Scope::Signal;

let signal_set: BitFlags<Scope> = signal.into();

let signal_uds = make_bitflags!(Scope::{Signal | AbstractUnixSocket});

let scope_v6 = Scope::from_all(ABI::V6);

assert_eq!(signal_uds, scope_v6);
```

--------------------------------

### Create Ruleset with Only Scope Restrictions

Source: https://docs.rs/landlock/0.4.3/src/landlock/lib.rs.html

This snippet demonstrates creating a ruleset that only applies scope restrictions for abstract Unix sockets and signals, without any file system or network access rules.

```rust
check_ruleset_support(
            ABI::V6,
            Some(ABI::V6),
            move |ruleset: Ruleset| -> _ {
                Ok(ruleset
                    .scope(Scope::AbstractUnixSocket | Scope::Signal)?
                    .create()? 
                    .restrict_self()?)
            },
            false,
        );
```

--------------------------------

### Test Scope Handling in Ruleset

Source: https://docs.rs/landlock/0.4.3/src/landlock/ruleset.rs.html

Tests the `scope` method for defining and handling scopes within a ruleset, comparing behavior across different Landlock ABI versions and verifying scope composition.

```rust
let scopes = make_bitflags!(Scope::{AbstractUnixSocket | Signal});

// Tests Ruleset::scope() with ABI that doesn't support scopes.
let ruleset = Ruleset::from(ABI::V5).scope(scopes).unwrap();
assert_eq!(ruleset.requested_scoped, scopes);
assert_eq!(ruleset.actual_scoped, BitFlags::<Scope>::EMPTY);

// Tests Ruleset::scope() with ABI that supports scopes.
let ruleset = Ruleset::from(ABI::V6).scope(scopes).unwrap();
assert_eq!(ruleset.requested_scoped, scopes);
assert_eq!(ruleset.actual_scoped, scopes);

// Tests composition (binary OR) of scopes.
let ruleset = Ruleset::from(ABI::V6)
    .scope(Scope::AbstractUnixSocket)
    .unwrap()
    .scope(Scope::Signal)
    .unwrap()
    .scope(Scope::AbstractUnixSocket)
    .unwrap();
assert_eq!(ruleset.requested_scoped, scopes);
assert_eq!(ruleset.actual_scoped, scopes);

// Tests that only the required scopes are reported as incompatible:
```

